  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustaining Education and Learning</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project is a follow-up to the ongoing Restoring Education and Emergency Learning (REAL) project, which is set to conclude in June 2025. The Sustaining Education and Learning Project&apos;s primary objective will be to sustain gains achieved under the REAL project in the coming school years while continuing to strengthen system capacity amid the ongoing conflict. Specifically, the project will support school rehabilitation, including construction of new classrooms to alleviate overcrowding, and the building of water, sanitation, and hygiene (WASH) facilities. Additionally, the project will provide school grants to targeted schools to support essential school expenditures, using a targeting index to prioritize interventions and following strict Entry Criteria of Access (ECA) for selecting beneficiary schools. Furthermore, to improve local institutions capacity for data collection, analysis and planning, the project will support data collection for one new school.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen Yemen&apos;s capacity to sustain basic education and learning in Targeted Schools.</narrative>
  </description>
